   "evidence": "The proof uses `Multiset.induction_on` and in `| cons a t _ =>` applies `hJc a t` and `hJ a t` at that single decomposition only (the induction hypothesis is discarded, `_`), so the universal quantifier is strictly more than the proof consumes; lines 505-511.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Jets/Observable/Recombination.lean",
   "fix": "Weaken to what the physics can supply: at minimum `\u2200 s \u2260 0, \u2203 a t, s = a ::\u2098 t \u2227 ContinuousAt (fun v => J (v ::\u2098 t)) a \u2227 \u2200\u1da0 p in \ud835\udcdd 0, J (p ::\u2098 a ::\u2098 t) = J (R.merge a p ::\u2098 t)`; faithfully, let the absorbing pseudojet depend on `p` (`\u2200\u1da0 p in \ud835\udcdd 0, \u2203 a \u2208 s, J (p ::\u2098 s) = J (R.merge a p ::\u2098 s.erase a)`, plus continuity at each member), which needs a finite split over the members of `s`. Keep `tendsto_cons_of_merge_zero` as the pointwise step.",
   "issue": "`IsUnital.isInfraredSafe` assumes `hJ`/`hJc` at *every* decomposition (`\u2200 (a : V) (t : Multiset V)`), i.e. the soft momentum is absorbed exactly into whichever pseudojet you name. No sequential-recombination observable with momentum values satisfies that: merging a soft `p` into the wrong jet changes jet momenta exactly, and which jet absorbs `p` depends on the direction of `p`. So the stated milestone counterpart on the infrared side is inapplicable to the Layer 2 observables it is aimed at, even though it is true (witness `Multiset.sum`).",
   "line": 501
  }
 ],
